# pipeline-ui's own secrets, read by bin/pipeline after the pipeline's (PIPELINE_ENV), so a value
# here wins. Copy to .env (gitignored) on each machine; never commit .env.
#
# Jira, for a queued ticket's summary and the console's ticket search. A scoped Atlassian API
# token: Jira takes it only through api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/<cloudId>.
# All three are needed; the console links a ticket key to JIRA_BASE_URL/browse/KEY.
# JIRA_BASE_URL is the site with its scheme, such as https://your-site.atlassian.net.
JIRA_BASE_URL=
JIRA_EMAIL=
JIRA_API_TOKEN=
# Optional: the site's cloud id (read from the site's /_edge/tenant_info when unset).
# JIRA_CLOUD_ID=
#
# Not secrets, but per machine too: the branch a run starts from and its pull request goes to
# (default master; it must have the entry point, so dev while webui's master does not), and
# whether a run may push and open its pull request (default on; off for a machine's first runs).
# PIPELINE_BASE_BRANCH=dev
# PIPELINE_PULL_REQUESTS=off
#
# The console's address (default 0.0.0.0, all interfaces). It has no password: on a server, keep
# the port behind a firewall or set 127.0.0.1 and open it through an SSH tunnel.
# PIPELINE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PIPELINE_PORT=8787
